The transverse components are different. Following the primed-frame and sign convention used on the board, $\begin{aligned}
  F'^{02}
  &=\gamma\bigl(F^{02}-vF^{12}\bigr), \\
  E'_2
  &=\gamma(E_2+vB_3).
  \end{aligned}$ A transverse electric component acquires part of a magnetic component. The remaining transformation laws follow from the same two-index rule and are left as the lecture’s exercise.

